%[text] # Biosciences: Genetics
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_053613DF] ## Information
%[text] This curriculum module contains interactive [MATLAB® live scripts](https://www.mathworks.com/products/matlab/live-editor.html) that analyze genetic data. 
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_F00D98E4] ### Background
%[text] You can use these live scripts as demonstrations in lectures, class activities, or interactive assignments outside class. This module covers calculating the statistics of a single DNA sequence, uses real genetic data to create a phylogenetic tree, and explores within-species genetic variation. 
%[text] This module utilizes data pulled from [GenBank](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/genbank/), the NIH's library of publicly available genetic sequences.
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![](text:image:1a87)
%[text]{"align":"center"} [A 3-dimensional model of DNA](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bdna_cropped.gif)
%[text] An internet connection is needed for GenBank sequence retrieval and the initial download of the primates example. Downloaded data belongs in `Data/` and is excluded from version control. Population data is simulated locally.
%[text] The instructions inside the live scripts will guide you through the exercises and activities. Get started with each live script by running it one section at a time. To stop running the script or a section midway (for example, when an animation is in progress), use the ![Stop icon](text:image:9db4) Stop button in the **RUN** section of the **Live Editor** tab in the MATLAB Toolstrip.
%[text] ### Contact Us
%[text] Contact the [MathWorks Educator Content Development Team](mailto:onlineteaching@mathworks.com) if you would like to request assistance, provide feedback, or if you have a question.
%[text] ### Prerequisites
%[text] This module assumes basic MATLAB knowledge and it is recommended that all students take the [MATLAB Onramp](https://matlabacademy.mathworks.com/details/matlab-onramp/gettingstarted).
%[text] ## Getting Started
%[text] To learn more about opening and using MATLAB, see the accompanying [Getting Started](http://gettingstarted.pdf) guide. 
%%
%[text] #### Accessing the Module
%[text] Use MATLAB R2025a or newer for these plain-text live scripts. For MATLAB R2024b or older, download the [legacy `.mlx` release](https://github.com/MathWorks-Teaching-Resources/Biosciences-Working-With-Data/releases/tag/mlx).
%[text] #### **On MATLAB® Online**™:
%[text] Use the [![Open in MATLAB Online Button](text:image:972d)](https://matlab.mathworks.com/open/github/v1?repo=MathWorks-Teaching-Resources/biosciences-genetics&project=BiosciencesGenetics.prj&file=README.m) link to download the module. You will be prompted to log in or create a MathWorks account. The project will be loaded, and you will see an app with several navigation options to get you started.
%[text] #### **On Desktop:**
%[text] Download or clone this repository. Open MATLAB, navigate to the folder containing these scripts and double-click on [BiosciencesGenetics.prj](<matlab: openProject("BiosciencesGenetics.prj")>). It will add the appropriate files to your MATLAB path and open an app that asks you where you would like to start. 
%[text] Ensure you have all the required products ([listed below](internal:M_5d15)) installed. If you need to include a product, add it using the Add-On Explorer. To install an add-on, go to the **Home** tab and select  ![Add-ons icon](text:image:94a4) **Add-Ons** \> **Get Add-Ons**. 
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_5d15] ## Products
%[text] MATLAB®, Bioinformatics Toolbox™, and the Statistics and Machine Learning Toolbox™ are used throughout. The Mapping Toolbox™ is used for `changem()`.
%[text] ## Scripts
%[text] Notes: These scripts can all be run independently, though we recommend going through these live scripts in order. These live scripts are intended to be used with output inline. To change the output, go to the View tab of the toolstrip, and select ![live script output inline icon](text:image:1a69) Output Inline. The scripts have areas for the students to interact with the code ![Try this icon](text:image:1f9d). 
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_F887EB68] ### [Explore a single DNA sequence](<matlab: edit Scripts/S1ExploreSingleDNASequence.m>)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,262,185],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![](text:image:06f5) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet$  import and analyze DNA sequences in MATLAB, and visualize nucleotide content</p> | <p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet$ Biology</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_00AECAD6] ### [Comparative genetics](<matlab: edit Scripts/S2ComparativeGenetics.m>)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,262,185],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | <p></p><p>![](text:image:3f60)</p> | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet$ calculate genetic distances between species</p><p>$\\bullet$ visualize genetic distance using phylogenetic trees</p><p>$\\bullet$ use genetic data to interpret evolutionary relationships</p> | <p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet$ Biology</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
