%[text] %[text:anchor:H_A3FE16AB] ## **Further Resources for students**
%[text]         1\) [an example of phylogenetic trees using the primate dataset](https://www.mathworks.com/help/bioinfo/ug/building-a-phylogenetic-tree-for-the-hominidae-species.html)
%[text]         2\) [an example of using phylogenetic trees to understand a disease](https://www.mathworks.com/help/bioinfo/ug/analyzing-the-origin-of-the-human-immunodeficiency-virus.html)
%[text]         3\) [more on sequence statistics](https://www.mathworks.com/help/bioinfo/ug/calculating-and-visualizing-sequence-statistics.html)
